{B.8.b20.28 = 28-34}
28.	A fox demanded of @wDN{Enlil} the horns of a wild bull. 
29.	While it was wearing the wild bull's horns, it started to rain. 
30.	But the horns rose high above him, so he could not enter his burrow. 
31.	Until midnight the wind kept blowing, and the clouds brought rain. 
32.	Afterwards, when it had stopped raining on him, and he had dried off, 
33.	he said: 
34.	@q{“I shall return this feature to its rightful owner!”} 

